l/agent/claude/testdata/real_error_max_turns.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_error_max_turns.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_success.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/real_success.meta.json\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_agent_quotes_limit.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_api_retry_killed.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_api_retry_recovered.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_credits_required.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_opus_text.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_rejected_event.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_resets_ms.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_limit_warning_only.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_throttle_not_usage_limit.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_truncated.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_usage.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_usage_limit.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/testdata/synthetic_windows.jsonl\ninternal/agent/claude/windows_test.go\ninternal/agent/errors.go\ninternal/agentjob/admit.go\ninternal/agentjob/admit_test.go\ninternal/agentjob/command.go\ninternal/agentjob/doc.go\ninternal/agentjob/job.go\ninternal/agentjob/job_test.go\ninternal/agentjob/snapshot.go\ninternal/agentjob/snapshot_test.go\ninternal/agentjob/testdata/snapshot.golden\ninternal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go\ninternal/botcheck/doc.go\ninternal/budget/budget.go\ninternal/budget/budget_test.go\ninternal/budget/notice.go\ninternal/budget/notice_test.go\ninternal/budget/testdata/repo.golden\ninternal/budget/testdata/role.golden\ninternal/budget/testdata/unpriced.golden\ninternal/cli/app.go\ninternal/cli/cli_test.go\ninternal/cli/cmd_config.go\ninternal/cli/cmd_init.go\ninternal/cli/cmd_labels.go\ninternal/cli/cmd_rebuild.go\ninternal/cli/cmd_serve.go\ninternal/cli/cmd_version.go\ninternal/cli/log.go\n386-**Branch protection and the bot.** The committer pushes `.ard/<issue#>/` commits straight to `main` with `[skip ci]`, which neither a \"require a pull request\" rule nor a required status check can admit, so the App must be on the bypass list of `main`'s ruleset (mode Always). GitHub's bypass covers the whole ruleset, not single rules (found on Gate 2, #39). ard keeps that bypass narrow itself: the committer refuses any path outside `.ard/<issue#>/`, the merger merges only when every review passed and required checks are green on the current head (checked in code, not left to GitHub), and the bot-commit audit flags any bot commit on `main` that touches anything else. GitHub enforces nothing on the App's merges, so the merger reads the required checks itself from the branch rules API. A squash merge has GitHub (`noreply@github.com`) as committer and the App as author, so the audit, which keys on the committer, does not cover merges: the merger's gates do.\n387-\n388:## Configuration\n389-\n390-Configuration is by convention: a role exists because its directory exists, and `.ard/config.yaml` holds only global settings and overrides. No prompt path is written anywhere; ard reads `.ard/<type>/<name>/prompt.txt`. Model credentials are host settings (`ARD_AGENT_AUTH`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the `ard serve` environment), not `config.yaml` keys, because a PR can change `config.yaml`.\n391-\n392-```\n393-.ard/\n394-├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\n395-├── scanners/<name>/     # scan (executable) or prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n396-├── triage/<name>/       # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n397-├── workers/<name>/      # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n398-├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n399-└── <issue#>/            # per-issue output and logs, written only by the committer\n400-```\n401-\n402-- A directory with `prompt.txt` is an agent role; a scanner directory with an executable `scan` is a deterministic scanner.\n403-- A `Dockerfile` builds the role's image; without one the local executor runs a host subprocess and the Kubernetes executor uses the default `ard-agent` image (agent CLIs, git, common linters). A role that reads untrusted input without one triggers the host-mode warning (see Executors and the Reaper).\n404-- Any other file in the directory (scripts, allowlists) is mounted read-only beside the prompt.\n405-\n406-```yaml\n407-max_pods: 3                  # job slots shared by every loop\n408-executor: local              # local | k8s\n409-agent: claude                # default CLI for agent roles\n410-require_approval: true       # human adds ard:approved before a worker starts\n411-budget_usd_per_day: 50       # whole repo, UTC day, blocks at spent >= cap; a role may set its own; provisional, recalibrated between Gate 1 and Gate 2\n412-max_budget_usd: 5            # per job; provisional, same recalibration\n413-global_max_open: 30          # open scanner issues across all scanners\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"613d0aa5-60ce-4d1b-910e-4573476cfa86","uuid":"98a90d36-1d7b-4b8b-bf1d-32710262fff6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:30:10.590Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"CLAUDE.md\nDockerfile\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\ncmd\ndeploy\ndocs\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\n.dockerignore\n.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\n.github/workflows/ci.yml\n.gitignore\nCLAUDE.md\nDockerfile\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\ncmd/ard/main.go\ncmd/ard/main_test.go\ndeploy/argocd/Chart.yaml\ndeploy/argocd/templates/instances.yaml\ndeploy/argocd/values.yaml\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/Chart.yaml\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/templates/_helpers.tpl\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/templates/deployment.yaml\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/templates/externalsecret.yaml\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/templates/networkpolicy.yaml\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/templates/pvc.yaml\ndeploy/charts/ard-serve/values.yaml\ndeploy/cosign.pub\ndeploy/test-charts.sh\nde